 [17592186152208 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186373511 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186152208 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186375487 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186152208 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186375494 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186152208 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Complement of an Intersection" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186152208 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186152016 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186152208 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "be98b214-0860-51c6-930b-756af86ec330" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186152378 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186153136 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186152378 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186153137 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186152378 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186153138 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186152378 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186153139 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186152378 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186152378 #edb/ref 1045 "De Morgan's Laws for Sets" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186152378 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186153138 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186152378 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048734 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186152378 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "f3693137-83df-50ce-b9df-4844eb6a3b95" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186153136 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186153137 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186153136 #edb/ref 1061 26657 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186153136 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7a08f22c-b7bc-5e1e-9190-e2abe659a937" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186153136 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186152207 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186153137 #edb/ref 1061 26658 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186153137 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "71f338d8-0b25-55b4-8e2d-8edc82c4cf14" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186153137 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186152208 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186153138 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186153139 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186153138 #edb/ref 1061 26659 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186153138 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1f2c991b-1f17-5ca9-b2bb-adab88ae5d59" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186153138 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186153401 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186153139 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186153136 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186153139 #edb/ref 1061 26660 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186153139 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a0df9dac-82ec-5e01-9bea-92f979e60ec8" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186153139 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186153402 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186153401 #edb/ref 1064 "**De Morgan's laws** for sets tell us alternative ways to represent the complement of a union or intersection.\n\n- De Morgan's law for unions states that $$\\overline{A \\cup B} \\equiv \\overline{A} \\cap \\overline{B}.$$\n- De Morgan's law for intersections states that $$\\overline{A \\cap B} \\equiv \\overline{A} \\cup \\overline{B}.$$\n\nIntuitively, you can think that the complement \"flips\" the union into an intersection and vice versa.\n\nTo demonstrate De Morgan's laws, consider the sets $A = \\{ 1,2,3 \\}$ and $B = \\{ 3,4 \\}$ in the universe $U = \\{ 1,2,3,4,5,6 \\}.$\n\n- Computing $\\overline{A \\cup B},$ we have $$\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A\\cup B} & =\\overset{―}{{1,2,3}\\cup {3,4}} \\\\ & =\\overset{―}{{1,2,3,4}} \\\\ & ={5,6}.\\end{aligned}$$ Computing $\\overline{A} \\cap \\overline{B},$ we have $$\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A}\\cap \\overset{―}{B} & =\\overset{―}{{1,2,3}}\\cap \\overset{―}{{3,4}} \\\\ & ={4,5,6}\\cap {1,2,5,6} \\\\ & ={5,6}.\\end{aligned}$$ So, we have that $\\overline{A \\cup B} = \\overline{A} \\cap \\overline{B}. \\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n- Computing $\\overline{A \\cap B},$ we have $$\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A\\cap B} & =\\overset{―}{{1,2,3}\\cap {3,4}} \\\\ & =\\overset{―}{{3}} \\\\ & ={1,2,4,5,6}.\\end{aligned}$$ Computing $\\overline{A} \\cup \\overline{B},$ we have $$\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A}\\cup \\overset{―}{B} & =\\overset{―}{{1,2,3}}\\cup \\overset{―}{{3,4}} \\\\ & ={4,5,6}\\cup {1,2,5,6} \\\\ & ={1,2,4,5,6}.\\end{aligned}$$ So, we have that $\\overline{A \\cap B} = \\overline{A} \\cup \\overline{B}. \\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186153401 #edb/ref 1065 4366 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186153401 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "df8a49e7-15bf-53b1-9af3-754dbf9fc0e8" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186153401 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186153402 #edb/ref 1064 "For the sets $A = \\{ 1,2,3 \\}$ and $B = \\{ 3,4 \\}$ in the universe $U = \\{ 1,2,3,4,5,6 \\},$ the region $\\overline{A \\cup B} = \\overline{A} \\cap \\overline{B}$ is shown below:\n\n![](images/36/367abce6d3386da347ab0eae5cb2d60110c3c642f7a679b6b8b8070e417fc10c.png)\n\nLikewise, the region $\\overline{A \\cap B} = \\overline{A} \\cup \\overline{B}$ is shown below:\n\n![](images/b0/b0a876470b3d2bd455395667f4d0221f73ee7c16dbbb20027a114c356638bc2d.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186153402 #edb/ref 1065 4367 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186153402 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "3dc144c9-c8b9-50c4-a923-43e5b8574041" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186153402 #edb/ref 1067 "Venn Diagram Representations of De Morgan's Laws" #edb/ref 17592186045585]}
